<title>USA: British Telecom to buy MCI, CNBC says; stock halted.</title>
<headline>British Telecom to buy MCI, CNBC says; stock halted.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc is in negotations to buy the remaining 80 percent of MCI Communications Corp. it does not already own, television channel CNBC said Friday.</p>
<p>Trading in MCI's stock was halted, the Nasdaq market said just after 1:30 p.m. EST.</p>
<p>&quot;MCI ... is in negotiations to be bought by its 20 percent owner Britsh Telecom, and sources close to the deal tell me it could be announced as early as Monday morning,&quot; a CNBC reporter said.</p>
</text>
